Package: MultipleSystemsEstimation
Title: Methods for Multiple Systems Estimation
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
  given = c("Bernard", "W."),
  family = "Silverman",
  email = "bernard.silverman@stats.ox.ac.uk",
  role = c("aut", "cre") ),
    person("Lax", "Chan",
           role = "ctb"),
    person("Kyle", "Vincent",
           role = "ctb")
    )
Description: Methods for multiple systems estimation using
  Poisson log-linear models, with particular attention to sparse capture
  data, model selection and its associated uncertainty, and Bayesian
  thresholding of interaction effects. The package implements methodology
  from Silverman (2020) <doi:10.1111/rssa.12505>,
  Chan, Silverman and Vincent (2021)
  <doi:10.1080/01621459.2019.1708748>, and Silverman, Chan and Vincent
  (2024) <doi:10.1007/s11222-023-10346-9>.
URL: https://bernardsilverman.github.io/MultipleSystemsEstimation/,
        https://bernardsilverman.co.uk/contact
